# S236 v2: S097's mate row re-mined on the flipped tree, 2026-09-23.
#
# WHY. DEC-231's one pre-registered follow-up halves the fractional history
# term's reach -- LmrHistClamp 2048 -> 1024 -- and on that tree the row
# "pruning does not hide a forced mate" carried for S097 verdict 2,
# 4N3/8/3P1ppk/4p2p/4P2P/1n1P2P1/Q4PK1/3q4 w - - 5 46 at depth 14, distance 5,
# stopped being true of the shipped build: mate_found is false there. The same
# row survived S236 v1 at clamp 2048; it is the flip that turned it false. A
# golden whose derivation moved is re-derived by its own script (DEC-142), the
# way S188 did for this very row and the way S236 v1 did for S095's.
#
# WHAT RAN. adocs/data/S097_mine_mate_row.py's stages 2 to 6, kept at
# .tuning/coord/S236v2_remine_s097.sh:
#   * stage 1 is not re-run: the 269 candidates are the corpus and the oracle,
#     neither of which moved, and adocs/data/S097_candidates.tsv still holds it
#   * both sweeps at depths 11 to 14 -- the range the script derives from
#     SeMinDepth and does not write out -- one against this tree's engine
#     library, one against a library built with E21 applied out of tree, the
#     source reverted against its own sha between them
#   * the separator set derived from the two sweeps, the firing witness run
#     over it on the tune library at SeMultiCut 0 and 1, and the pick
#
# THE RESULT, and the pick rule had nothing to choose between:
#
#   1 of 269 candidates separates the two sweeps on this tree.
#
#   take: 2r4r/kq3pb1/N3p1p1/QPp1Pn1p/2PPRP2/7P/5BP1/R5K1 w - - 1 31
#     depth 14, mate in 6, shipped [d11 d12 d13 d14], guard dropped
#     [d11 d12 d13], fires [d14], 38927874 nodes, 4536 ms
#
# The cell costs 38927874 nodes and about 4.5 s against the 0.65 s of the row it
# replaces. That is what this corpus charges for a depth-14 mate that separates
# here; the script's cheaper-cell tie-break never came up because only one
# candidate qualified, and the cost is recorded rather than traded away.
#
# Oracle, fresh process through chess.engine.SimpleEngine at depth 20:
# #+6 for White in 70199 nodes, pv Nxc5+ Kb8 Nxb7 Rxc4 Qb6 Kc8 Nd6+ Nxd6 Ra8+
# Kd7 Qxd6#; python-chess reports the position valid, not in check, 38 legal
# moves, two captures, no promotion.
#
# Red observed with E21 applied by hand and green with it reverted, sha
# checked: .tuning/coord/S236v2_observe_red.log. The row it replaces stays in
# the case's GOLDEN block with the tree it belongs to, so an H0 on S236 v2 is a
# revert and not a third re-mine.
#
# ==== the pick, as the script printed it ====
